{"case": {"case_id": "2025-EP-00400", "case_type": "estate_intestate", "parties": {"decedent": {"full_name": "Arthur P. Melanson", "address": "412 Pine Street, Portland, ME 04103", "phone": "207-555-0182"}, "spouse": {"full_name": "Eleanor R. Melanson", "address": "412 Pine Street, Portland, ME 04103", "phone": "207-555-0183"}, "applicant": {"full_name": "Thomas J. Melanson", "relationship_to_subject": "Son", "address": "88 Ocean Avenue, Falmouth, ME 04105", "phone": "207-555-0191"}, "personal_representative": {"full_name": "Thomas J. Melanson", "relationship_to_subject": "Son", "address": "88 Ocean Avenue, Falmouth, ME 04105", "phone": "207-555-0191"}}, "facts": {"bond_required": true, "testacy": "intestate", "spouse_surviving": true, "real_estate_in_estate": true, "has_minor_heirs": false}, "narrative": "Decedent Arthur P. Melanson died intestate on November 15, 2024. Although survived by his spouse Eleanor R. Melanson, the surviving spouse has filed a written waiver of priority for appointment. The decedent's adult son, Thomas J. Melanson, petitions to serve as Personal Representative. Under Maine probate law, a non-spouse PR is required to post a surety bond unless the court waives it for cause. The estate includes residential real property in Portland and liquid assets. Thomas J. Melanson will be required to secure a bond prior to the issuance of Letters of Administration.", "party_lists": {}, "extra_parties": {}}, "event": {"case_id": "2025-EP-00400", "type": "decedent_death_date", "date": "2024-11-15", "details": "Decedent passed away at MaineMedical Center, Portland. Death certificate filed with Cumberland Registry of Vital Records."}, "id": "estate_intestate_bond_req_400", "description": "Synthesized estate_intestate case", "scenario": "bond_required"}
{"case": {"case_id": "KEN-2024-EP-00892", "case_type": "estate_intestate", "jurisdiction": "Maine Probate Court, Kennebec County", "status": "active", "parties": {"decedent": {"full_name": "Arthur J. Levesque", "attrs": {"last_known_address": "14 Maple Ridge Rd, Augusta, ME 04330"}}, "applicant": {"full_name": "Elena M. Levesque", "relationship_to_subject": "spouse", "address": "14 Maple Ridge Rd, Augusta, ME 04330", "phone": "207-555-0142"}, "personal_representative": {"full_name": "David R. Levesque", "relationship_to_subject": "son", "address": "88 Pine St, Waterville, ME 04901", "phone": "207-555-0198"}, "minor": {"full_name": "Sophie L. Levesque", "relationship_to_subject": "daughter"}, "attorney": {"full_name": "Margaret T. O'Connell", "address": "225 Water St, Portland, ME 04101", "phone": "207-555-0211", "attrs": {"bar_number": "ME-88421", "firm": "O'Connell & Partners LLC"}, "email": "m.oconnell@mainelaw.com"}}, "facts": {"pr_removal_petitioned": true, "testacy": "intestate", "spouse_surviving": true, "has_minor_heirs": true, "real_estate_in_estate": true}, "narrative": "Arthur J. Levesque died intestate, survived by his spouse Elena and two children, including a minor daughter. His adult son David was initially appointed personal representative to administer the estate. Following repeated failures to file statutory accountings and allegations of commingling estate funds with personal accounts, the surviving spouse has filed a petition to remove David as PR for cause. The estate includes the family homestead in Augusta and liquid assets requiring supervised administration for the minor heir.", "party_lists": {}, "extra_parties": {}}, "event": {"type": "pr_removal_filing", "case_id": "KEN-2024-EP-00892", "date": "2025-06-12", "description": "Petition to remove personal representative filed by surviving spouse alleging breach of fiduciary duty, asset mismanagement, and failure to comply with Maine Probate Code accounting requirements."}, "id": "estate_intesta